{"title":"2025 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 6","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2_-_Creativity_💡\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2 - Creativity 💡</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Solution_4\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 4</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Solution_5\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 5</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Solution_6\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 6</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#Solution_7\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">8</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 7</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-9\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_Daily_Dose_of_Math\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">9</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by Daily Dose of Math</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-10\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_DDM\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">10</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by DDM</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-11\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_Continuum_Math\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">11</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by Continuum Math</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-12\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_1_by_Math-X_(First_fully_understand_the_problem!!!)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">12</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution 1 by Math-X (First fully understand the problem!!!)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-13\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_2_by_Cool_Math_Problems\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">13</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution 2 by Cool Math Problems</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-14\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_3_by_SpreadTheMathLove\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">14</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution 3 by SpreadTheMathLove</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-15\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_4\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">15</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution 4</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-16\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_5_by_Thinking_Feet\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">16</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution 5 by Thinking Feet</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-17\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution(Quick,_fast,_easy!)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">17</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution(Quick, fast, easy!)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-18\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_SquishBJ_(AIME_Qualifier)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">18</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by SquishBJ (AIME Qualifier)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-19\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_in_Chinese_by_SquishBJ_(AIME_Qualifier)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">19</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution in Chinese by SquishBJ (AIME Qualifier)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-20\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">20</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Sekou writes the numbers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/c/6/ec6b6717c568b97fd4e049dae3583b33a0a665a7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$15, 16, 17, 18, 19.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"130\" height=\"17\" /> After he erases one of his numbers, the sum of the remaining four numbers is a multiple of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/b/1/cb15a16cca90d201094265ee529e9e2cfb113de8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> Which number did he erase?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/2/0/220517774eaf5af7114d40925c605cfe64c9e257.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ 15\\qquad \\textbf{(B)}\\ 16\\qquad \\textbf{(C)}\\ 17\\qquad \\textbf{(D)}\\ 18\\qquad \\textbf{(E)}\\ 19$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"397\" height=\"18\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The sum of all five numbers is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/7/9a7e85308970b82c5b944f85a302c9f6541c96d6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$85. Since$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"71\" height=\"14\" />85 is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/3/b/d3bad2f5a97dc56a8a06dd0459df91940aafe110.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1 more than a multiple of$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"188\" height=\"18\" />4, the number being subtracted must be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/3/b/d3bad2f5a97dc56a8a06dd0459df91940aafe110.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1 more than a multiple of$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"188\" height=\"18\" /><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/9/b/19b3fa4aa82ef1689a4b7bcb750ad1ea59864e46.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$. Thus, the answer is$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"155\" height=\"16\" />\\boxed{\\text{(C)}~17}$. ~Gavin_Deng\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_2_-_Creativity_.F0.9F.92.A1\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2_-_Creativity_💡\">Solution 2 - Creativity 💡</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2 - Creativity 💡\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Notice the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/6/fc606f7f1e530731ab4f1cc364c01dc64a4455ee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />'s place as you erase one number; you get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/8/7/78792fe4680a164f537ea72a4f900e4471433c3b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$40$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />, which is a multiple of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, so you can ignore the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/6/fc606f7f1e530731ab4f1cc364c01dc64a4455ee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />'s place in the numbers provided altogether because it will always be a multiple of 40. This means that the only relevant numbers are the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />'s digit ones. If you add the numbers now, you get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/3/e/e3e6e9f972f93bda8c0f87e04cfd6f217965d429.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5+6+7+8+9=35.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"184\" height=\"15\" /> The closest multiple of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> underneath <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/7/8c7f6c79f2148f0cec592c9517b40ee1b82ef22e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$35$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> which can be achieved as a result of subtracting either <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/1/601a7806cbfad68196c43a4665871f8c3186802e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/a/e0a0db32027a732ac57d37ef2ae9bb150f65b108.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/5/8455f3b5cb3b4880b8c9d782a5c1f0334db819eb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/2/bf2c9074b396e3af0dea52d792660eea1c77f10f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/2/6/9265f5dd6dade78136a6be158ace46bf7c0f8ce3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$28$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />, which is achieved by subtracting <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/a/e0a0db32027a732ac57d37ef2ae9bb150f65b108.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, therefore the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/6/5/a6519d00e02ff3bf31fb28ed06b8b5110c43b598.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(C)}~17}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"65\" height=\"30\" />.\n</p><p>~firethinkz\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3\">Solution 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The sum of the residues of these numbers modulo <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/f/0/cf05a79bf80d0a88df2c6519dfa16edd8ab394c5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-1+0+1+2+3=5 \\equiv 1 \\pmod 4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"289\" height=\"20\" />. Hence, the number being subtracted must be congruent to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> modulo <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. The only such answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/6/5/a6519d00e02ff3bf31fb28ed06b8b5110c43b598.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(C)}~17}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"65\" height=\"30\" />.\n</p><p>\\(\\textbf{Note}\\): To those who are confused about why, for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/1/9/f1965fae079a9ba2c0726c307070c2355dfcb213.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$15$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />, it said the residue modulo <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/a/e/bae5aba07d37ff6ff813107e76260fb31ad5794e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"25\" height=\"15\" />  instead of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> (because of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/f/edf074831eb5bc9e61d6d6e09f525a86e3068f6a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$12$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />), look here. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/5/e25a5cfe55036e7687311343bc94d6d5934ed306.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-1 \\equiv 3 \\pmod 4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"131\" height=\"20\" />. The same principle above applies even if you replace <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/a/e/bae5aba07d37ff6ff813107e76260fb31ad5794e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"25\" height=\"15\" /> with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />; two numbers are in the same residue class if their difference is a multiple of the modulus ( \\(3-(-1)=4\\), which is \\(1\\times 4\\) ). \n</p><p>~cxsmi\n</p><p>~note by i_am_not_suk_at_math\n</p><p>~minor <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/latex.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\LaTeX$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"46\" height=\"15\" /> fixes by i_am_not_suk_at_math\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_4\">Solution 4</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 4\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The sum of all the numbers here is equivalent to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/1/a/f1afd603eef50072f609e671bcb62cc4d5f2cbdb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$17 \\cdot 5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"42\" height=\"14\" />. Subtracting 17 gives us <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/c/d/9cdfdb7a3a65fb263d2e089e1e6f3b46f9068e8a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$17 \\cdot 4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"42\" height=\"14\" />, which is clearly a multiple of 4. Therefore, the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/6/5/a6519d00e02ff3bf31fb28ed06b8b5110c43b598.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(C)}~17}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"65\" height=\"30\" />.\n~themathkidwoohooooo\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_5\">Solution 5</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 5\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Since the sum of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/a/8/aa8b9ef2a72cf6763a1f08d8eb322d9640171f81.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$15 + \\dots + 19$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"104\" height=\"15\" /> is odd, we immediately exclude B and D. We further note that if A is true, then E is true. Hence, the answer is C.  \n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_6\">Solution 6</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 6\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We can use the fact that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/9/1/9912596152140f8dc08c47fe3f58d8cce38dcb10.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(a + b) \\mod n = [(a \\mod n) + (b \\mod n)] \\mod n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"414\" height=\"20\" />. Notice that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/b/9/7b9cd2c58901673a2e1972acad773b4e8a06a638.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$15, 16, 17, 18, 19$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"125\" height=\"17\" /> dividing by 4 have remainders <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/b/9/3b9af4b9236dd1c9c4a4f6f6052e9e7174706594.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3, 0, 1, 2, 3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"80\" height=\"17\" />. Their sum is 9. It is easy to see that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/7/9/779dec1fa400d67f5413e527177df80f6d027f65.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9-1=8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"76\" height=\"15\" /> is divisible by 4 and so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/6/5/a6519d00e02ff3bf31fb28ed06b8b5110c43b598.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(C)}~17}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"65\" height=\"30\" /> is the correct answer.\n</p><p>~minor edit by themathkidwoohooooo, just fixed the LaTeX for the answer\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_7\">Solution 7</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 7\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>If we use brute force and add <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/1/6/716ce5a5f47e2f34e9373302484f65022d3920bc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$15+16+17+18+19$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"182\" height=\"15\" />, we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/f/e/7fea07b9bf739f8e420081f31186264b91ced2ce.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$85$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />. When we subtract every number from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/f/e/7fea07b9bf739f8e420081f31186264b91ced2ce.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$85$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />, we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/a/9/aa94edfb9739dcc66dad90f7dd5c148f44a57e2c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$70$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/8/0/a80952a9a250e7257f7c6d64e763dae189dbb271.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$69$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/7/8/9782dd7447f84ce6adcf7945b86038e379c618f2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$68$\" width=\"17\" height=\"12\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/f/a/7fa7247f4d29d95459cbf6f238007a1b1090ebea.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$67$\" width=\"18\" height=\"12\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/d/4/2d40f3652c1962e98ce050a88c04ed37997c67df.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$66$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />, we see that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/7/8/9782dd7447f84ce6adcf7945b86038e379c618f2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$68$\" width=\"17\" height=\"12\" /> is divisible by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/6/5/a6519d00e02ff3bf31fb28ed06b8b5110c43b598.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(C)}~17}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"65\" height=\"30\" /> is the correct answer.\n</p><p>~VersatileGopher38\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_Daily_Dose_of_Math\">Video Solution by Daily Dose of Math</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=9\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by Daily Dose of Math\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"//youtu.be/nkpdskFVgdM\">~Thesmartgreekmathdude</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_DDM\">Video Solution by DDM</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=10\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by DDM\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/so5BcuYaoYc\">https://youtu.be/so5BcuYaoYc</a>\n</p><p>~piggydude\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_Continuum_Math\">Video Solution by Continuum Math</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=11\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by Continuum Math\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/gHGif8Ut7Qo&amp;t=4\">https://youtu.be/gHGif8Ut7Qo&amp;t=4</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Video_Solution_1_by_Math-X_.28First_fully_understand_the_problem.21.21.21.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_1_by_Math-X_(First_fully_understand_the_problem!!!)\">Video Solution 1 by Math-X (First fully understand the problem!!!)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-edi